\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a surjective morphism $f:X\to Y$ of smooth projective varieties over a field of characteristic zero, with connected fibers and general fiber $F$, must the Kodaira dimensions satisfy
\[\kappa(X)\geq\kappa(Y)+\kappa(F)?\]
The Kodaira dimension measures the asymptotic growth of pluricanonical sections; the question is ordinary Iitaka subadditivity.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2022/32}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For a surjective morphism $f:X\to Y$ of smooth projective varieties over a field of characteristic zero, with connected fibers and general fiber $F$, must the Kodaira dimensions satisfy
\[\kappa(X)\geq\kappa(Y)+\kappa(F)?\]
The Kodaira dimension measures the asymptotic growth of pluricanonical sections; the question is ordinary Iitaka subadditivity.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30005169 (OWR-11101913-003). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2022/32}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:30005169}

